Its other steps (defective pixel correction, color and tone, the
post-filter) port Omarchy Mobile's own libcamera changes, released under the
LGPL-2.1-or-later, which allows their use under the GPL.

The omacam binary links these Rust crates statically, each under its own
license: libcamera and libcamera-sys (MIT OR Apache-2.0), gtk4, gdk4, gsk4,
glib, gio, libadwaita and the other gtk-rs crates (MIT), turbojpeg
(Unlicense OR MIT), and the crates listed in Cargo.lock. It links libcamera
(LGPL-2.1-or-later), GTK and libadwaita (LGPL-2.1-or-later) and
libjpeg-turbo (BSD-3-Clause, IJG) dynamically.
